<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI6-IMPORTANT-FINDINGS>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI6-IMPORTANT-FINDINGS" ;
  triage:title "AI6-QA-1 Important findings (non-blocking, fix promptly)" ;
  triage:description "Grouped non-blocking findings: (1) OpenAPI document advertises /teams and /team/{teamName} endpoints with no router correspondence; (2) Contract test only checks YAML parseability, never validates router request/response against schema; (3) AuthenticatedIngress passed as unused _ingress parameter — Local/Peer distinction never consulted by routing logic; (4) Stale docs in architecture.md + boundaries.md still describe retired RpcEnvelope/frame-codec; (5) LoopbackClientTransport not cfg(test)-gated, ships in production atm-core library; (6) Error-cause swallowing at ~15 HTTP-over-UDS I/O boundaries (AtmError::daemon_unavailable swallows real io::Error); (7) Duplicated daemon_local_ipc_name_from_path diverging between atm-daemon-client and atm-core; (8) try_connect_with_traceability returns Result<bool, AtmError> but can never Err (dead fallibility at 4 call sites); (9) Hardcoded /tmp/atm-daemon.sock in doc example/test literal (cross-platform-guidelines grep gate)." ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "REQ" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-20T16:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s6/764bdd32> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-s6/764bdd32> ;
  triage:reviewedBy "req-qa" ;
  triage:reviewedBy "rust-qa-agent" ;
  triage:reviewedBy "rust-best-practices-agent" ;
  triage:reviewedBy "ruthless-boundary-qa" ;
  triage:notes "UPDATED at feature/pAI-s6-http-uds-router @ e50d67f1 (AI-FIXROUND-4), independently verified by quality-mgr: now 7 of 9 sub-items PASS (or PASS-with-caveat) — (2) contract test upgraded to real route↔schema-declaration correspondence: openapi_declares_the_implemented_doctor_exchange (crates/atm/src/commands/api.rs:55-73) calls production endpoint_for() and asserts the real method+path exists in the OpenAPI doc with a declared responses.200 schema; caveat: does not deserialize/validate an actual response body's field values against that schema, so full body-schema validation is still absent; (3) AuthenticatedIngress genuinely matched in runtime_health.rs:777; (4) docs/architecture.md:247-253 and docs/atm-daemon/boundaries.md:249-267 now correctly describe the current ApiRequest/ApiResponse/ApiRouter architecture, retired RequestDispatcher family explicitly marked historical; (6) AtmError (crates/atm-storage/src/error.rs:9-53) now has a real cause: Option<String> field plus with_cause/daemon_unavailable_with_cause constructors backed by test adapter_cause_is_preserved_without_changing_the_error_code; spot-checked 5+ call sites in atm-daemon-client/src/lib.rs (362-366, 370-375, 464, 796-803, 811-818) all now pass the real source through instead of discarding it; (7) daemon_local_ipc_name_from_path deduped; (8) try_connect_with_traceability simplified to plain bool; (9) hardcoded /tmp/atm-daemon.sock literal fully removed. 2 of 9 sub-items still FAIL: (1) OpenAPI /teams + /team/{teamName} PARTIAL — the OpenAPI YAML side is genuinely cleaned (zero hits for /teams or /team/ paths), but route_api_request() left orphaned dead code: crates/atm-core/src/api.rs:350-356 route_is_teams() still matches /v1/atm/teams and /v1/atm/team/{name}, api.rs:97-113 decode_request() still special-cases them into ApiRequest::Teams, and runtime_health.rs:809-812 still explicitly errors with the now-FALSE message text \"daemon API route {} {} is declared in OpenAPI but team administration routing remains outside the AI.6 runtime router\" — stale/misleading dead code, not removed and not accurately re-labeled; (5) LoopbackClientTransport cfg(test) gate still FAIL, unaddressed by AI-FIXROUND-4 — real path is crates/atm-core/src/transport/mod.rs:1 (not atm-daemon as originally cited), still `pub mod testing;` with no cfg gate, LoopbackClientTransport (transport/testing.rs:51) remains a plain pub struct compiled into every production build. Finding remains OPEN pending these 2 sub-items." .

